1 0 0 1 50 585 Tm
(• The virus is an ultramicroscopic \(20-300 nm in diameter\),) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 563 Tm
(metabolically inert, infectious agent that replicates only) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 541 Tm
(within the cells of living hosts, mainly bacteria, plants and) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 519 Tm
(animals; composed of an RNA or DNA core, a protein coat) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 497 Tm
(and in more complex type, a surrounding envelope.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 475 Tm
(• The protein coat is known as capsid and its subunit is) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 453 Tm
(known as capsomere.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 431 Tm
