1 0 0 1 50 299 Tm
(in 1892. He found that a disease of tobacco plants could) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 277 Tm
(be transmitted by an agent, later called tobacco mosaic) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 255 Tm
(virus, passing through a minute filter that would not allow) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 233 Tm
(the passage of bacteria.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 211 Tm
(• In 1898, Martinus Beijerinck independently replicated) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 189 Tm
(Ivanovsky’s filtration experiments and then showed that) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 167 Tm
(the infectious agent was able to reproduce and multiply) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 145 Tm
(in the host cells of the tobacco plant. He coined the term) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 123 Tm
(‘virus’.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 101 Tm
