(III. Fungal Diseases) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 673 Tm
(Notes) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 651 Tm
(• The Fungi are a separate kingdom of living things.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 629 Tm
(• A fungus \(plural fungi\) is a kind of living organisms; yeast,) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 607 Tm
(moulds \(molds\) and mushrooms are types of fungi.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 585 Tm
(• Fungi have cells with nuclei \(eukaryotic organisms\).) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 563 Tm
(• Fungus cell wall contains chitin unlike the cell wall of) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 541 Tm
(plants, which contain cellulose.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 519 Tm
(• Most fungi grow as tubular filaments called hyphae. An) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 497 Tm
(interwoven mass of hyphae is called a mycelium. The) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 475 Tm
(walls of hyphae are often strengthened with chitin, a) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 453 Tm
(polymer of N-acetylglucosamine.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 431 Tm
(• The study of fungi is called Mycology.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 409 Tm
(• All fungi are heterotrophs either parasitic or saprotrophs.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 387 Tm
(• Fungi have a close relation to humans. Several species of) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 365 Tm
(fungi are useful and harmful to humans.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 343 Tm
(• Some main fungal infections have been described as) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 321 Tm
(below :) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 299 Tm
(Aflatoxins :) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 277 Tm
(• Aflatoxins are a family of toxins produced by certain fungi) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 255 Tm
(that are found on agricultural crops such as maize, peanuts,) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 233 Tm
(cotton seeds and tree nuts.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 211 Tm
(• The main fungi that produce aflatoxins are Aspergillus) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 189 Tm
(flavus and Aspergillus parasiticus, which are abundant) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 167 Tm
(in warm and humid regions of the world.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 145 Tm
(• Aflatoxin-producing fungi can contaminate crops in the) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 123 Tm
(field, at harvest, and during storage.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 101 Tm
(• Aflatoxin is a natural carcinogen which is associated with) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 79 Tm
(an increased risk of liver cancer.) Tj
