1 0 0 1 50 563 Tm
(spp. can cause disease directly, but other organisms can) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 541 Tm
(cause disease by the toxins that they produce.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 519 Tm
(• The most important parasitic diseases are as follows–) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 497 Tm
(Malaria :) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 475 Tm
(• Malaria is a life-threatening disease. It is typically) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 453 Tm
(transmitted through the bite of female Anopheles) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 431 Tm
(mosquito. Infected mosquitoes carry the Plasmodium) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 409 Tm
(parasite. When this mosquito bites, the parasite is released) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 387 Tm
(into the bloodstream. The primary host of Plasmodium is) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 365 Tm
(a man and the secondary host is female Anopheles.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 343 Tm
(• Once the parasites are inside the body, they travel to the) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 321 Tm
(liver, where they mature. After several days, the mature) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 299 Tm
(parasite enters the bloodstream and begin to infect red) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 277 Tm
(blood corpuscles \(RBCs\).) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 255 Tm
(• Within 48 to 72 hours, the parasites inside the red blood) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 233 Tm
(corpuscles multiply, causing the infected cells to burst) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 211 Tm
(open.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 189 Tm
(• The parasites continue to infect red blood cells, resulting) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 167 Tm
(in symptoms that occur in cycles that last two to three) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 145 Tm
(days at a time.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 123 Tm
(• Malaria is typically found in tropical and subtropical) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 101 Tm
(climates where the parasites can live.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 79 Tm
(• There are four kinds of malaria parasites that can infect) Tj
